20:T6cc,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What does RTO stand for?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Regional Transport Office. It is the state government office that registers vehicles and issues driving licences in a region."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the tool show vehicle owner details?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Owner information is not public through this tool. Use the official Parivahan or Vahan services for permitted checks."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are all RTO codes covered?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The database covers more than 1,200 codes, but new offices are added by states over time, so a recent code may be missing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I transfer my vehicle to another state?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, by obtaining an NOC from your current RTO and re-registering in the new state within the permitted period."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get vehicle owner details from the number plate?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Owner details require the official Vahan portal. Our decoder only identifies state and RTO code from the plate format."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the RTO Finder free on ContentVerse India?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. All India utility tools on ContentVerse India are free to use with no sign-up required."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this an official government website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. ContentVerse India is an independent platform. We use public datasets and open APIs. For official records, use government portals like Parivahan, GST, FoSCoS, or ECI."}}]}21:T7c8,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"How to use RTO Finder","description":"Every vehicle registered in India carries a state and RTO code that identifies the Regional Transport Office that registered it. This RTO finder lets you search more than 1,200 RTO codes by city, district or state and shows the office name and address. Use it to find the RTO code for a city, identif","url":"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/rto-finder","totalTime":"PT5M","tool":{"@type":"HowToTool","name":"RTO Finder"},"step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"How to use the RTO finder","text":"Type a city name, a district or a code such as MH12 or UP25 in the search box. The results show the RTO code, office name and address where available. Add the state name or code to your search if a city name appears in more than one state."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"How RTO codes work","text":"A standard registration number looks like MH12AB1234. The first two letters stand for the state or union territory, the next two digits identify the RTO or district office within that state, followed by one to three letters for the series and a four-digit number. The RTO code usually maps to a city or district, such as 12 for Pune in Maharashtra."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"What you can do at an RTO","text":"RTOs handle new vehicle registration, renewal of registration, transfer of ownership, driving licences, fitness certificates, permits and No Objection Certificates. Many of these services have moved online on the Parivahan portal, so check whether you can complete the task without a visit."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"BH series and special plates","text":"The Bharat (BH) series lets people who move frequently between states, such as defence personnel and some private-sector employees, keep one registration number across India. BH plates do not follow the state-and-RTO format and instead use a year, BH, a number and letters."}]}16:[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebApplication\",\"name\":\"RTO Finder\",\"alternateName\":\"RTO Code Finder — Vehicle Registration Office India\",\"description\":\"Search 1,200+ RTO codes by city or state with office address across India.\",\"url\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/rto-finder\",\"applicationCategory\":\"UtilitiesApplication\",\"operatingSystem\":\"Any\",\"browserRequirements\":\"Requires JavaScript\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"0\",\"priceCurrency\":\"INR\"},\"provider\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"ContentVerse India\",\"url\":\"https://contentverse.co.in\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-IN\",\"featureList\":\"How to use the RTO finder, How RTO codes work, What you can do at an RTO, BH series and special plates\"}"}}],["$","script","1",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$20"}}],["$","script","2",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"India Tools\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"RTO Finder\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/rto-finder\"}]}"}}],["$","script","3",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$21"}}]],"$L22"]
